inks":[["Pushmataha County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/oklahoma/pushmataha-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, Pushmataha County has 75 years of record on its 13 grids, from 1951 to 2025. On the middle of the grids, August to September and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 37 of those years. In 2025 the middle ran 157% of normal in April to May and 51% of normal in September to October. Grid 17240 had its driest year in 1963, at 54% of normal.</p>"}
